T’was as day like no other, it was unusually windy in the high tree city of the wood elf’s. But neither the less it was a happy day for 2 residence in the higher less visited city area. For this was the day that there child was born. It was noted early in his life that this child was not all too bright and would need help to do most of the simple tasks that both rangers and druids would have, so it was no surprise that the local war guild was more then happy to except him as a possible recruit. But Wolas as he was later know (it was the warrior guild leader himself that said that he is intelligent as a wall that he was known as wolas) was more found of nature and the beautiful noises within the forest. Wolas was not as smart as most wood elf’s his age but the gift of song was apparent with him. So as he came of age he decided to leave his steal welding brothers and attempt to join the local bard’s guild, it was a long and hard battle to get accepted into the order of the bards. But he managed to plead his case to the guild leader who saw mercy in his eye and allowed him to train. With his poorly crafted drum wolas took his first steeps into the wild slaying both large and small intruders who dare pass on his domain, with his gift of song he strengthened groups healed hurt comrades and traveled faster then any wolf in the land. It was around the time of the 10th song that wolas was told to go to Freeport on a simple boat ride to pick up some mail he was also told that it was there that he will find his 10th song, as wolas was headed thought the land of dwarf’s he found a small vile looking creature that was slowly killing the dwarfs as bright as wolas was he approached the small elf like form and spoke to him, 
Wolas: Hail 
Dark elf:  why do you intrude on my hunting ground small one 
	  Is it riches you seek? 
Wolas:     I am on a mission from the great city of the wood elves 
	  But I might have time to seek a few gold.
Dark elf:	  then take this note to a human named Taldarron 
	  In the land of commons he will reward you 
Wolas:    All right 

It was then that was embarked on his first adventure. It was only 2 days later that wolas reached the land of commons and found a human with an ugly vile looking creature hanging by his side 

Wolas:   	          Taldarron I bring you a note from a Vile elf in the 
	          Dwarf land
Taldarron:        I thank you small one and I will reward you!

With a swift command he made his undead companion vanish and after a few moments he began to chant and an even move VILE ugly creature in the form of death itself appeared, Taldarron seemed pleased 

Taldarron:	take this bag and give it to a small gnome near the caves of the            Minos He will reward you even greater 

With that Taldarron handed wolas a small bronze BP and Greaves, Wolas was pleased it was his first armor that he did not need to rip of an Orc scum.  As wolas head back to Freeport a since of pride filled him he had gotten his song and the bag of mail and was headed on a boat back to his home land where he was egger to show off his new armor. As wolas passed is home he dropped off the bag of mail and was commended on his armor and rewarded with a small bit of coin, he used this to buy a new drum and to run as fast as his legs would take him to the land of the gnomes, it was there near the mino caves that he found his target the gnome looked as if he had a great Weight on his shoulders but was most happy to take the bag given by wolas, the small man reached into his bag and said “ You have traveled long and far you have gotten armor fitting your age and now you will hold a weapon the will protect you and pride for may years to come” with that the gnome reached into his bag and pulled out a great weapon whose power was felt when weld , the gnome said it was a long battle that won him that blade and that it will hit as hard as any blade of the veteran bards, ( kilij 15/35 magic ) with that a great shield with the color of a great spider followed in his other hand but that was not all , to wolas’s feet the gnome strapped on a shiny blue plate as well as to his hands , to his arms more bronze showed and to his head wolas was given a hood the gleamed with eh power of an  executer. As wolas walked to his home he was no longer looked upon as a hopeless wood elf that would need help thought out this life but more as a great bard that has earn the respect of his peers and the power of his armor and weapons.
